iterations.reply:
I left out the enrichment fetch to `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=...`. This node's `with` clause grants only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`, which is its entire authority. Calling that URL would need `aap:caps/http-client`, and importing it would widen the node's authority beyond what the graph grants. It would also send the customer's question to a host outside the node's scope. If you need enrichment, the graph should grant it, for example a separate node holding `HTTPClient<['metadata.internal.example']>`.

The build errors are fixed by importing `AgentResponse`, `LlmError` and `Intent` from `crate::aap::caps::types`.

